  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The length of the semi-major axis of the elliptical orbit of the planet is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>If we assume that there is a hypothetical planet which moves around the sun in a circular orbit of radius&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>, then the time period of this hypothetical planet and our given planet will be same. The time period of a planet around the sun in&nbsp;circular orbit is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><msqrt><mfrac><msub><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mi>G</mi><msub><mi>M</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><msqrt><mfrac><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>3</mn></msup><mrow><mi>G</mi><msub><mi>M</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><msqrt><mfrac><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>3</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>G</mi><msub><mi>M</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math></p>",
